					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: CONVERSION\n\nIn this example we use a Float In at Event flow to control the Circle.\nWe use the Trigger node to convert the changes in the Float In node to a trigger.\nThe trigger is then used to generate a random color for the Circle.\n\nNote that this conversion is for demonstration purposes.\nThe Random node will implicitly convert the event float to trigger itself.\nYou can try this out by removing the trigger from the patch and connecting the Radius directly to the Random. Using conversion nodes however, can sometimes be beneficial to the readability of your patch."
					}
				},
